WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.600
Good day, bad day, by Paul Shipton. Penguin Active Reading Easy Start.

00:10.700 --> 00:19.300
Mike gets a new job and moves from his small town to Boston. 

00:19.400 --> 00:26.200
He likes the job, and he likes his new apartment. 

00:26.300 --> 00:29.400
He likes Boston. 

00:29.500 --> 00:33.400
There is only one problem. 

00:33.500 --> 00:37.790
He doesn't meet many new people.

00:37.840 --> 00:49.000
This weekend, Mike's sister, Carrie, is visiting her brother. 

00:49.300 --> 00:54.800
Do you have many new friends here? 

00:54.900 --> 00:56.600
She asks him. 

00:56.700 --> 01:02.630
Not many, Mike says.

01:02.680 --> 01:08.700
I'm worried about you, Carrie says. 

01:08.800 --> 01:15.800
You're always worried about me, Mike says. 

01:15.900 --> 01:20.400
On Saturday morning, they go out. 

01:20.500 --> 01:26.400
Let's go into town, Mike says. 

01:26.500 --> 01:30.500
There's a bus stop near here. 

01:30.600 --> 01:36.900
But Carrie sees a sign in a window. 

01:37.000 --> 01:43.800
Visit Rosie, the fortune teller. 

01:43.900 --> 01:51.700
No, she says. Let's go in there. 

01:52.000 --> 01:56.000
Mike isn't happy about this.

01:56.100 --> 02:00.500
He doesn't believe in fortune tellers. 

02:00.600 --> 02:11.200
But Carrie says, please, Mike, I love fortune tellers. 

02:11.300 --> 02:23.200
Wait, Carrie, but she is going into the house and Mike can't stop her. 

02:23.500 --> 02:26.600
He goes in after her. 

02:26.700 --> 02:34.100
A woman is sitting at a table in a small room. 

02:34.200 --> 02:40.000
This is Rosie, the fortune teller. 

02:40.100 --> 02:48.200
Who is first? The woman asks. 

02:48.300 --> 02:53.270
I am, Carrie says.

02:53.520 --> 03:00.500
The two women go into a room at the back of the house. 

03:00.600 --> 03:04.400
Mike sits and waits. 

03:04.500 --> 03:13.750
After some time, Carrie comes back with a big smile on her face.

03:14.160 --> 03:20.600
Now you go, she says to her brother. 

03:20.700 --> 03:30.100
Mike isn't very happy about this, but he goes into the back room. 

03:30.200 --> 03:33.300
It is very dark. 

03:33.400 --> 03:42.600
Rosie smiles and puts some cards on the table in front of her.

03:43.600 --> 03:48.800
She looks at them for a long time. 

03:48.900 --> 03:52.800
She isn't smiling now. 

03:52.900 --> 03:58.900
What's the problem, Mike asks? 

03:59.000 --> 04:09.100
It is not a good day for you today, she says.

04:09.200 --> 04:17.600
Mike doesn't like this. Why not? He asks. 

04:17.700 --> 04:31.800
I can see a black cat, a yellow dog and a white bird. 

04:31.900 --> 04:36.300
Be very careful.

04:36.400 --> 04:42.550
On the street, Carrie asks Mike about the fortune teller. 

04:42.600 --> 04:55.550
A cat, a dog and a bird, she asks. Are you worried?

04:55.600 --> 05:01.100
No. I don't believe it, Mike says. 

05:01.200 --> 05:10.550
Fortune tellers are always wrong, but Carrie isn't listening to him.

05:10.600 --> 05:16.700
Mike, she says, look at that. 

05:16.800 --> 05:24.600
There is a cat near them, a black cat.

05:25.600 --> 05:30.900
Remember Rosie's warning, Carrie says. 

05:31.000 --> 05:36.100
Let's go across the street. Quick! 

05:36.200 --> 05:45.350
I am not worried about a little black cat, Mike says, 

05:46.450 --> 05:51.550
but he walks across the road with Carrie.

05:51.600 --> 05:59.700
There, a man is washing a cafe window with a bucket of water. 

05:59.800 --> 06:05.000
Suddenly, the bucket falls. 

06:05.100 --> 06:12.550
All of the water in it falls too. On, Mike.

06:12.600 --> 06:16.800
I'm sorry. The man says. 

06:16.900 --> 06:25.900
Remember the fortune tellers warning, Carrie says quietly. 

06:26.000 --> 06:28.300
Her eyes are big.

06:29.000 --> 06:33.100
Look at the name on the sign. 

06:33.200 --> 06:37.300
The black cat cafe. 

06:37.400 --> 06:44.550
I do not believe in fortune tellers, Mike says.

06:44.600 --> 06:50.800
But look at me. Let's go home. 

06:50.900 --> 06:59.600
But then Carrie says, no. Mike, look. 

06:59.700 --> 07:10.550
Mike looks and sees a big dog, a big yellow dog.

07:10.600 --> 07:13.500
It is running at him. 

07:13.600 --> 07:21.300
Mike can't believe his eyes. Oh no, he thinks. 

07:21.400 --> 07:27.550
Is the fortune tellers warning right?

07:27.600 --> 07:31.050
But the dog doesn't stop. 

07:31.100 --> 07:33.600
It runs past him. 

07:33.700 --> 07:38.600
There is a big smile on Mike's face. 

07:38.700 --> 07:46.550
Now do you believe me? Mike wants some food now.

07:46.600 --> 07:51.100
He buys a hot dog on the street. 

07:51.200 --> 07:57.600
But Carrie is thinking about the fortune teller.

07:58.600 --> 08:04.650
Wait, she says. A hot dog. 

08:04.700 --> 08:12.600
Maybe that's the dog in the fortune tellers warning.

08:13.600 --> 08:19.300
Yes, but it isn't yellow, Mike says. 

08:19.600 --> 08:30.550
Mike is looking at his sister and he doesn't see the little boy near him.

08:30.600 --> 08:35.800
Be careful. The boy's mother says. 

08:35.900 --> 08:45.200
But Mike walks into the boy and a toy falls from the boy's hands. 

08:45.300 --> 08:49.550
It hits the road and breaks.

08:49.600 --> 08:54.500
The boy looks down at the little parts of the toy. 

08:54.600 --> 09:01.600
He is very unhappy. The boy's mother is angry.

09:02.000 --> 09:10.600
Toys are very expensive, she says to Mike.

09:11.000 --> 09:21.600
I'm sorry, Mike says. Here, please take this money for a new toy.

09:22.000 --> 09:27.600
But Carrie is looking at the boy's old toy. 

09:27.700 --> 09:32.600
Look, Mike, she says.

09:33.600 --> 09:38.800
The toy is a little yellow dog. 

09:38.900 --> 09:43.100
Mike's face is white. 

09:43.200 --> 09:46.550
Now he is worried too.
 
09:46.600 --> 09:54.600
Now do you believe the fortune teller? Carrie asks.

09:55.600 --> 09:59.800
Maybe Mike says quietly. 

09:59.900 --> 10:04.600
He is walking quickly now.

10:05.600 --> 10:09.500
Where are we going? Carrie asks. 

10:09.600 --> 10:16.600
Home, he says. He looks up.

10:17.600 --> 10:22.600
What are you looking for? Carrie asks. 

10:22.700 --> 10:25.800
But she knows the answer. 

10:25.900 --> 10:28.600
Her brother is worried.

10:29.600 --> 10:34.100
He is looking for a white bird. 

10:34.200 --> 10:39.000
Suddenly, Mike hears a noise. 

10:39.100 --> 10:42.600
He looks behind him.

10:43.600 --> 10:46.900
A woman is running after him. 

10:47.000 --> 10:53.600
Excuse me. The woman calls. 
 
10:54.600 --> 10:57.800
Yes, Mike says. 

10:57.900 --> 11:03.700
My name's Sally. The woman says. 

11:03.800 --> 11:11.600
I'm new here. The black cat cafe is my cafe.

11:12.600 --> 11:15.650
She looks at Mike's shirt. 

11:15.750 --> 11:21.600
I'm very sorry about that bucket of water.

11:22.600 --> 11:26.500
My friend is working at the cafe today. 

11:26.600 --> 11:30.900
He isn't always very careful. 

11:31.000 --> 11:34.600
That's okay, Mike says.

11:35.600 --> 11:43.600
It is hot today. Sally smiles at him.

11:44.600 --> 11:50.600
She has a beautiful, friendly smile, Mike thinks.

11:51.600 --> 12:00.600
Listen, he says. Maybe we can go out to a movie this evening?

12:01.600 --> 12:08.600
Okay, yes, Sally says. Let's meet at the cafe.

12:11.600 --> 12:20.500
Sally is walking back to the cafe, but suddenly Carrie calls to her.

12:20.600 --> 12:27.900
Wait, Sally, she says. What's your family name?

12:28.600 --> 12:31.600
Sally looks back.

12:32.600 --> 12:40.600
Swan, she says. My name is Sally Swan.

12:41.600 --> 12:45.100
And then she goes into her cafe. 

12:45.200 --> 12:51.600
Mike looks at Carrie, and Carrie looks at Mike.

12:52.600 --> 13:01.100
That's bad, Carrie says. That's very bad. 

13:01.200 --> 13:07.600
A swan is a bird, and it's usually white.

13:08.800 --> 13:14.100
It's part three of your warning from the fortune teller. 

13:14.200 --> 13:18.600
You can't go to a movie with Sally.

13:19.600 --> 13:22.600
But Mike isn't worried. 

13:22.700 --> 13:26.500
He is putting his hot dog down. 

13:26.600 --> 13:29.600
He stands and waits.

13:30.600 --> 13:34.600
Carrie can't believe her eyes.

13:35.600 --> 13:39.600
What are you doing? She asks.

13:40.600 --> 13:44.600
Suddenly she hears a noise.

13:45.600 --> 13:49.500
A big seagull flies down. 

13:49.600 --> 13:56.200
It takes the hot dog, and then it flies away.

13:56.600 --> 14:01.600
I don't understand, Carrie says.

14:02.600 --> 14:05.600
Now you have no food.

14:06.600 --> 14:09.600
Mike is smiling.

14:10.600 --> 14:16.500
That seagull is a white bird, he says.

14:16.600 --> 14:21.600
Now the fortune teller's warning is right.

14:22.600 --> 14:29.500
A black cat, a yellow dog, and a white bird.

14:29.600 --> 14:35.600
And now I can go to a movie with Sally.

14:36.600 --> 14:40.500
Carrie smiles too.

14:40.600 --> 14:45.600
That fortune teller is good, she says.

14:46.600 --> 14:49.600
Why, Mike asks.

14:50.600 --> 14:57.600
Look at this. This is from Rosie, for me.

14:58.600 --> 15:01.600
(Thank you)
